# The relays this repository's releases start a new feeder from (RFC-0180 §4): the release's
# `seeds`, which packaging/install.sh reads (its header says the format) and tally-feed compiles in
# (crates/feed, `config::SEEDS`, so the binary and the image start from it too), checked by
# `install.sh --check-seeds`. One relay a line, HOST:PORT=KEY and the operator who runs it. Relays
# other operators run join this list as they come; until it names more than one operator, Tally's
# entry point is one operator's. A relay is listed only while its operator follows the network's
# rules for relay operators (docs/relay-operators.md): a receiver's exact site stays on relays and
# never reaches a client; public surfaces show only its public cell, about 5 km across.
